## Menu text

- Language names come from the Unicode Common Locale Data Repository (CLDR 49), © Unicode, Inc., under the Unicode License v3: `licenses/Unicode-3.0.txt`.
- OK, Cancel, Apply, Close and Reset to Defaults use Qt's own translations, which are part of Qt (below).
- Bible book names in the menus come from the book name lists of these Bibles' sources (eBible.org, CrossWire and thiagobodruk/bible).
- The rest of the menu text in languages other than English is machine translated. Corrections are welcome: https://github.com/puretechteam/bible-widget/issues

## Software in the download

The download (`BibleWidget-<version>-win64.zip`) is built from:

- Python 3.13, under the Python Software Foundation License, with the libraries it lists (libffi among them): `licenses/Python.txt`.
- Qt 6.10 and Qt for Python (PySide6 and Shiboken6 6.10.1), under the GNU Lesser General Public License v3, which builds on the GNU General Public License v3: `licenses/LGPL-3.0.txt` and `licenses/GPL-3.0.txt`. They are used unchanged. Qt's libraries sit in the download's `_internal` folder; PySide6's Python part is packed into `BibleWidget.exe`. To use your own build of them, rebuild the download from this app's source code (https://github.com/puretechteam/bible-widget, with `build.py`). Their source code is at https://download.qt.io/official_releases/qt/6.10/ and https://download.qt.io/official_releases/QtForPython/pyside6/. The third-party code inside Qt (HarfBuzz, FreeType, libpng, PCRE2, zlib and others) is listed with its licenses in `licenses/Qt-third-party.txt`.
- The Microsoft Visual C++ runtime, redistributed under Microsoft's terms for it.
